# Production build env, committed on purpose.
#
# These are the PUBLIC client analytics vars (VITE_-prefixed → baked into the
# browser bundle and therefore already visible to anyone who views source).
# They live here so EVERY production build picks them up — not just Vercel
# (which also has them as project env vars), but the iOS/Capacitor build too.
#
# WHY (David 2026-06-14): the iOS build runs `npm run build` in Xcode Cloud,
# which has NO access to Vercel's project env vars, so the native bundle shipped
# with PostHog as a no-op and the app went dark in analytics after 2026-06-13.
# Vite auto-loads .env.production in production mode; real process.env vars
# (Vercel) still take precedence, and the values here match prod exactly, so
# there is no divergence — this purely backfills the iOS build.
#
# Do NOT put secret keys here (DeepSeek/Anthropic/PostHog personal read key).
# Those are server-side only and must never be VITE_-prefixed or committed.
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_wQfkAaN8Tsdzoa45WjCqsrd2xeEktVYzh9oivB9jcqvA
VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://chess-academy-pro.vercel.app/api/ph
